  [ARG ] the proof of the ordering
         note: h_1 >= rho(sigma M_2) > rho(M_2) = h_2, so the walls are the isosceles configurations and the strands are ordered by the opposite sides
         why : proved. sigma is an isometry fixing the pair, so sigma M_2 lies at distance |M_2 - q_2| from body 1; rho is concave on that ball, so its critical point M_1 is the unique maximum there, giving the first step. The second is that rho o sigma > rho on body 2's side. The concavity hypothesis is an explicit inequality checked in scripts/concavity_lemma.py

