PARAGRAPH 6: frame independence
==============================================================================
  [PASS] frame independence
         note: viewed from six frames rotating at different rates the vineyard braid is the same
         got : six frames -> {'s2^-1 s1 s2^-1 s1'}
  [ARG ] why frame independence holds
         note: a change of frame carries rho(x,t) to rho(g_t^-1 x, t), superlevel sets go to congruent ones, the diagram is untouched
         why : exact: rho_{gq}(x,t) = sum_i K(|x - g_t q_i|) = sum_i K(|g_t^-1 x - q_i|) = rho_q(g_t^-1 x, t); an isometry of the plane maps each superlevel set homeomorphically to the other's, so H_0 and the pairing are identical

